  "caption": "The video captures a tennis ball dropping onto a racket strung with purple powder against a solid orange backdrop. Blurred by its speed, the ball descends from above and meets the horizontal string bed. On contact, the ball comes to rest against the mesh while the powder coating the strings begins to lift and billow upward. The viewpoint is a low, edge-on angle showing the racket's rim, with red, white, and black sections visible.\n\nAfter contact, the ball remains on the string bed and moves laterally toward the left side as the purple cloud thickens and expands, rising in soft plumes above the mesh and spreading across the upper area. The ball's blurred surface shows faint seam lines, and the powder forms a hazy trail around it. Meanwhile, the apparent angle of the racket changes from the initial edge-on view toward a more top-down perspective, revealing the oval string surface beneath the ball. Powder keeps dispersing into the orange background.\n\nThe ball moves upward and out of view, while the powder cloud continues rising into the orange air.",
